    <text type="letter">
        <body>
            <div type="writingSession">
                <pb n="1"/>
                <opener><fw place="left" type="adressline"><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3513"
                            type="person">Mrs. Alfred Neumeyer</rs>
                        <lb/>Friends of the Mills College Art Gallery<lb/><rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__860" type="place">Oakland</rs> 13, <rs
                            ref="#tillich_place_id__848" type="place">California</rs>.</fw>
                    <dateline><date when="1946-08-13">August 13, 1946</date></dateline><salute>Dear
                            <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__3513" type="person">Mrs.
                        Neumeyer</rs>:</salute></opener>
                <p>Many thanks for <rs ref="#L10952" type="letter">your letter</rs> and your
                        manuscript.<note type="ea">Liegt nicht vor.</note> The text you have
                    translated has meant very much to me about the period of the development of my
                    own political thinking.<note type="ea">Gemeint ist: <rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__1407" type="person">Novalis</rs>, <rs
                            ref="#tillich__E8B2N8XT" type="work">Die Christenheit und
                        Europa</rs>.</note> I of course would like to have an English translation
                    available in this country. I suppose that in the meantime you have received a
                    letter from a friend of mine, <rs ref="#tillich_person_id__752" type="person"
                        >Dr. <sic>Hannah</sic> Hafkesbrink</rs>, Head of the German Department in
                    Connecticut College. I believe that you should follow her advice. I myself am
                    sorry to say that I do not see any way for such a publication after an attempt
                    to give your manuscript to liberal Catholics which was without success.</p>
                <p>I would like to come once more to <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__848" type="place"
                        >California</rs> but I do not see how this can be done within a reasonable
                    time.</p>
                <closer><salute>With my best wishes</salute><salute>Yours sincerely, <lb/>Prof. <rs
                            ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Paul
                    Tillich</rs></salute></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
